<title>CANADA: Tee-Comm 21 pct stake in ExpressVu sold.</title>
<headline>Tee-Comm 21 pct stake in ExpressVu sold.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>ExpressVu Inc said on Monday that the 21 percent stake in it held by Tee-Comm Electronics Inc was purchased and was being held by a trustee pending regulatory approval of the acquisition of the stake by BCE Inc, WIC Western International Communications Ltd and/or Canadian Satellite Communications Inc. Details of the deal were not disclosed.</p>
<p>ExpressVu is a direct-to-home satellite television concern, licensed by the Canadian Radio-television and Telecommunications Commission, which plans to provide Canada satellite television service as an alternative to cable.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau  (416) 941-8100</p>
</text>
